U.S. stock benchmarks Thursday finished the day broadly higher, and the Dow Jones Industrial Average booked a 6th straight advance -- equaling its longest win streak in more than two months. Better-than-expected jobless claims and a slower pace of inflation supported equities, as particularly the latter suggested the Federal Reserve won't increase the pace of its monetary policy normalization any time soon. The Dow ended 0.8% higher at 24,739. The S&P 500 ended 0.9% higher at 2,723, marking a second day of gains, while the Nasdaq Composite Index had its fifth straight day of closing higher, ending up 0.9% at 7,405. In individual stocks, tech giant Apple Inc. (AAPL) rose 1.3% and hit a new record high.
-Anneken Tappe;
 10-18 1639ET
